Basic File Management:

ls:                    Lists files and directories in the current directory.
cd:                      Changes the current working directory.
pwd:                       Prints the current working directory.
mkdir:                         Creates a new directory.
rm:                       Removes files or directories.
cp:                           Copies files and directories.
mv:                             Moves or renames files and directories.
touch:                           Creates a new empty file. 

#Network and System Information:

ifconfig:                                     Displays network interface configurations.
ping:                                         Sends ICMP echo requests to test network connectivity.
netstat:                                       Displays network statistics and connections.
nmap:                                               Performs network scanning and port enumeration.
uname:                                           Displays system information.
whoami:                                       Displays the current user's name.
clear:                                         Clears the terminal screen. 

#Text Manipulation and Viewing:


cat:                                       Displays the contents of a file.
grep:                                   Searches for text within files or output.
head:                                   Displays the first lines of a file.
tail:                                     Displays the last lines of a file.
less:                                         Displays multi-page outputs.
find:                                     Locates files and directories based on various criteria.
tar:                                       Creates and extracts archives. 

#Advanced and Specialized Tools:

Metasploit:                                     A powerful penetration testing framework.
Aircrack-ng:                                     A tool for wireless network auditing.
John the Ripper:                                           A password cracking tool.
OWASP ZAP:                                             A web application security scanner.
Nmap:                                                   A network scanner.
Wireshark:                                           A network protocol analyzer.
Burp Suite:                                           A web application proxy.
Hydra:                                             A password cracker. 

#Other Useful Commands:

chmod:                                                     Changes file permissions.
man:                                                   Displays manual pages for commands.
echo:                                                   Prints text to the console.
top:                                                     Provides an ongoing view of processor activity. 
